ilver and 11  bronze  and the latest gold medal came in  women's hockey team canada defeated  their u.s rivals three to two the two  teams have met in all but one hockey  final since it was made an olympic sport  over two decades ago eric sorenson looks  back at their remarkable rivalry  it is as repetitive and predictable a  championship as you will find in sport  canada usa women's hockey but the  olympics is about excellence and what  these two teams have achieved is an  unparalleled competitive rivalry it came  down once more to this canada superstar  marie felipe scoring and in a fiercely  fought final canada winning  pulan has scored in the last four  olympic finals drawing comparisons to  legend haley wickenheiser this one in  particular is very special everybody  was so dialed in to be able to bring  back that gold medal and i think that's  what makes it so special canada may have  an edge historically but they are bitter  rivals who make each other better  women's hockey has been played in the  last seven winter olympics canada has  now won five gold medals the united  states the other two  to truly appreciate this unrivaled  duopoly in a single sport since the  women's world hockey championships began  in 1990 canada and the us have won every  title in the 27 world and olympic finals  finishing second to each other 25 times  the olympics are obviously a massive  stage and i think we showcased in this  tournament  you know the skill and and the speed at  which we're playing the game the  canadian women's game would not be what  it is without a worthy rival and vice  versa american hillary knight calls it  the best rivalry in sports hands down  it's wonderful she says the way we've  elevated this game and continue to  elevate the sport i think that's what  separates this rivalry because it's  happened so often and you see those two  things the excellence on the ice and the  pride in their country finland sweden  and other countries love hockey too but  must 